  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- Writing a vCard 3.0 or 2.1 card keeps a backslash followed by \"n\" in an ADR LABEL parameter as those two characters instead of writing a line break; only \"^n\" is a line break (RFC 6868).\n- VcardValue.TryParseUri and the typed URI members of a card give no Uri for a URI whose scheme is one letter, such as c:/dir/file, on every runtime, instead of a file URI on Windows; the card keeps the value as written.\n- VcardValue.TryFormatUri and the vCard values made from a Uri throw ArgumentException for a Uri made from a drive path, such as C:/dir/file, whose text would be read back as a URI with the scheme \"C\".\n- Writing a vCard 2.1 card now refuses a value or parameter that isn't valid in a card held by an `AGENT`, as it does in the card itself, unless `AllowInvalidValues` is set.\n- VcardReader throws VcardFileException (InvalidValue) for a vCard 2.1 QUOTED-PRINTABLE value on a line of 76 characters or more, which vCard 2.1 §2.1.3 doesn't allow; AllowInvalidValues accepts it.\n\nFixed:\n- The package now includes its XML documentation, so IntelliSense shows member descriptions.\n- Reading a vCard 3.0 or 2.1 card keeps a value that vCard 4.0 has no form for, instead of throwing InvalidOperationException.\n- Reading a vCard 2.1 or 3.0 AGENT whose card keeps a line in its own form no longer fails.\n- Writing a vCard 3.0 card reports the sort key of an ORG as lost when the card has an N, instead of moving it to the name.\n- Writing a vCard 3.0 card splits a quoted TYPE list into separate types instead of writing it as one type.\n- Writing a vCard 2.1 card no longer writes AGENT cards nested deeper than a reader accepts.\n- Reading a vCard 3.0 time keeps every digit of its fraction of a second instead of only the first 18.\n- VcardDate.TryParse gives the default date when it rejects an xCard year alone.\n- `VcardValue.TryParseFloat` gives 0, not infinity, when it rejects a number beyond the range of `double`.\n- The vCard 3.0 and 2.1 views show a REV, BDAY or TZ value that vCard 4.0 has no form for.\n- IVcard30Card.Labels and IVcard21Card.Labels give a backslash followed by \"n\" in an ADR LABEL parameter unchanged instead of as a line break.\n- VCard FLOAT and EMLX real values are read as the same double on .NET Framework as on .NET 10, including negative zero.\n- Writing a vCard 2.1 card under `AllowInvalidValues` no longer throws for a kept `QUOTED-PRINTABLE` value that can't be decoded; it is written as it is.\n- Writing a vCard 3.0 card with no N keeps the sort key of each ORG, as a SORT-STRING after it.\n- Reading a vCard 3.0 card with an N keeps a second SORT-STRING as a property of its own, instead of giving it to an ORG.\n- IVcard30Card.SortString gives only the sort string a vCard 3.0 writer writes, from the first N or, with no N, the first ORG.\n- On .NET Framework, XcardWriter and XcalWriter no longer report an asynchronous write as written when their stream or text writer cancels it.",
